<hr data-start=3D"416" data-end=3D"419">
<h3 data-start=3D"421" data-end=3D"470">=F0=9F=94=81 2. La riga con <code d=
ata-start=3D"443" data-end=3D"470">t =3D t || new Promise(...)</code></h3>
<p data-start=3D"472" data-end=3D"570">Qui si usa una <strong data-start=3D=
"487" data-end=3D"518">variabile globale o esterna</strong> chiamata <code =
data-start=3D"528" data-end=3D"531">t</code> (non =C3=A8 dichiarata dentro =
la funzione).</p>
<p data-start=3D"572" data-end=3D"589">Questa riga dice:</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"590" data-end=3D"700">
<p data-start=3D"592" data-end=3D"700">Se <code data-start=3D"595" data-end=
=3D"598">t</code> =C3=A8 gi=C3=A0 definita (e quindi =E2=80=9Ctruthy=E2=80=
=9D), usala.<br data-start=3D"641" data-end=3D"644">
Altrimenti crea una nuova <code data-start=3D"672" data-end=3D"681">Promise=
</code> e assegnala a <code data-start=3D"696" data-end=3D"699">t</code>.</=
p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start=3D"702" data-end=3D"788">Quindi <code data-start=3D"709" data=
-end=3D"712">t</code> viene <strong data-start=3D"719" data-end=3D"751">ini=
zializzata solo una volta</strong>, alla prima chiamata della funzione.</p>
